  "brief_rationale": "The doctor met the acute chest-pain responsibility chain: they elicited key symptom/vital details, reprioritized cardiovascular emergency risk over the lung nodule, escalated to 120/ED, gave transfer safety-netting, set medication boundaries, and obtained concrete family receipt. There were no serious or minor in-chain errors and no important non-chain defect; later advice remained bounded to ED discharge instructions, home return thresholds, and near-term chest-pain/cardiology follow-up. Multiple high-order opportunities were actively completed, including refusal navigation, lung-nodule misconception repair, adapted caregiver-facing communication, and dynamic escalation after red-flag details emerged. This supports grade 5.",
